# mutgap2_res_objlist_misaligned_by_one: SetObjectAndPlacementList (68)'s alignment test checks the offsets the previous accepted call stored, not the new ones (as tasks_objlist_placement shows): an object list at PAGE + 1 is accepted and stored, so the next call, a valid one, is refused for it and zeroes the offsets, and the call after that is accepted. The same for a placement list at 6 pages + 1, whose offset is stored only with argument buffers (the service): there the call after it is refused, in-process accepted. Each result shows in the task root.
